      "writtenOn": "2022-08-26T01:33:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s ultimately calling the general `connect` that is being modified in my last patch (7).\n\nI feel like we should not connect to profiles that aren\u0027t available (before this it connects to both a2dp and hfp regardless of that, though there were no callers of it).\n\nSo I find it natural to have a method to retrieve available audio profiles here, and check it upon `connect` and use it to compute missing profiles. Did you mean to suggest to move this function to the general Bluetooth layer instead (or move the check upwards)?",
      "parentUuid": "4160ec23_f30e4fcb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 519,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "c4cc913c2e0410ee6b873812194f30633b5aa95e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e74a9f9_5591e22e",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 519,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079709
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-26T02:07:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should only connect the profile available in UUID, for avoiding side effects.\n\nAnd it\u0027s interesting to know there\u0027s the `connect_all_enabled_profiles` in bluetooth.rs layer and it makes me wonder how stable does HFP-only device work since `MediaActions::Connect` is guarded by checking `A2DP` profile.\n\nHeadset could initiate profile connection, but if headset doesn\u0027t do that for some reason, it\u0027s host side\u0027s job to take care of it. \nIMO we should take care that logic in bluetooth.rs as a different CL/bug.",
      "parentUuid": "85b13ee7_7664315d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 519,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "c4cc913c2e0410ee6b873812194f30633b5aa95e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb628e55_eb463aeb",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 519,
      "author": {
        "id": 1543626
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-30T21:59:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re Jeremy:\nI was thinking about filtering the uuids in bluetooth.rs and pass the uuids to bluetooth_media.rs through the MediaActions::Connect. The get_remote_uuids interface you use here is the same one bluetooth.rs uses. It makes sense to me to put the audio_profiles filtering logic in the bluetooth_media.\n\nRe Hsin-Yu:\nAccording to my test, HM1000(HFP only headset) somehow also reports the A2dpSink uuid, making the HFP still work. I don\u0027t know if this is by design or there is other hidden issue for the reported UUID. We should be cautious when making the connection logic change from connecting \"all profiles we supported\" to \"only those reported\" and I do agree this should be a different CL/bug. I haven\u0027t seen any feedback report or encountered any issue regardingly so it has been a lower priority bug buried in my memory. The potential side effects you bring up could be a valid point to raise its priority.",
      "parentUuid": "6e74a9f9_5591e22e",
